  "description": "Retrospective change of use of an existing outbuilding to a small‑scale, appointment‑only nail treatment room (Class E). No external alterations are proposed. The outbuilding is an existing single‑storey structure within the rear garden of 49 Carlisle Road and retains its original form, materials, windows and door. The proposal relates only to the internal use of the space.\n\nThe nail treatment room operates strictly by appointment, with one client at a time and a maximum of 3–4 clients per day. Treatments are non‑invasive and low‑noise. No machinery, amplified music, or clinical/aesthetic procedures are used.\n\nClients arrive on foot or via public transport due to permit‑controlled parking on Carlisle Road. No dedicated parking is provided and no additional vehicle movements are generated. Access is via the existing side entrance and rear garden path.\n\nWaste generated is minimal, non‑hazardous and disposed of with household waste. No chemicals, liquids or clinical waste are produced.\n\nThe use is small‑scale, low‑impact and compatible with the residential character of the area, with no effect on neighbouring amenity, parking, noise levels or the appearance of the property.",
